  "notes": "Cash basis county, fiscal year ended June 30, 2025. Trimmed PDF has 9 pages (p1 Net Position, p2 Activities, p3 Assets and Fund Balances, p4 Receipts/Disbursements governmental funds, p5 General Fund combining, p6 non-major combining, p7 General Fund budget, p8 Road Fund budget, p9 budget note). Receipts/disbursements from Total Governmental Funds column p4. Taxes 1,088,134 split into property 1,035,907 and motor vehicle 52,227 using Statement of Activities general receipts (p2), which sum exactly. Local 181,761 is unlabeled (category other, review). Beginning/ending cash are fund balances (cash basis): beginning 1,241,718 (p4), ending cash 1,003,610 + restricted 51,630. Other financing 33,631 = sale of surplus 27,014 + insurance proceeds 6,617; transfers in/out 303,211 each. Roll-forward: 1,241,718 + 1,755,482 - 1,975,591 + 303,211 - 303,211 + 33,631 = 1,055,240. Balance sheet uses Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis p1 (restricted cash 121,656 there vs 51,630 on p3 fund statement; totals agree). Detail: General Fund uses the budgetary comparison schedule p7 (more detailed than p5 combining); its budget-basis actual receipts (1,395,574) differ from the statement (1,364,662) because it includes sale of surplus/insurance proceeds in Local and excludes the Inheritance Tax Fund; disbursements agree at 1,094,173 but function grouping differs from p4 (e.g. Miscellaneous 453,168 under General Government). Object breakdown not shown so expenditures are not itemized. Non-major combining p6 shows only four funds (Preservation & Modernization, Veteran's Aid, Library, Pre-Trial Diversion); other non-major funds (drug law enforcement, 911, etc.) appear on a page not in the trimmed PDF, so non-major detail is incomplete. Zero-valued lines omitted from non-major detail. Read pages 1-9 of 9."
